    "done_when": "§7's vessel-box paragraph is the specification. In imas_ambix/worldmodel/equilibrium_labels.py, xpoint_null_set and build_geometry_from_arrays take an optional in-vessel box (an R range and a |Z| bound) that _null_in_vessel uses. Its default is today's XPOINT_VESSEL_R_RANGE and XPOINT_VESSEL_Z_ABS, so every existing MAST caller and label is unchanged, and tests/worldmodel/test_equilibrium_labels.py and tests/test_equilibrium_labels.py pass unedited apart from new cases. imas_ambix/eval/efit_referee.py _selene_psrc_loader passes JT-60SA's box, derived from the limiter contour in the OP1 phase store's wall IDS, read through imas from /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/maps/jt-60sa/machine_description/OP1/wall.nc with imas_ambix/gs/artifact_geometry.py read_artifact_limiter. The box is the contour's R extent and |Z| extent, widened by the same margin MAST's box carries over its measured limiter extent (see the comment above XPOINT_VESSEL_R_RANGE), never typed by hand. A caller-supplied box keyword overrides it. New tests: in tests/eval/test_selene_reference.py, with a synthetic X-point inside JT-60SA's limiter at R of about 2.6 m, the loader's X-point slot is finite where MAST's default box would null it; a synthetic X-point outside JT-60SA's limiter is still nulled; and the derived box contains the whole OP1 limiter contour. In tests/worldmodel/test_equilibrium_labels.py, xpoint_null_set with an explicit box keeps a null the default box rejects. Write a landing fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-xpoint-vessel-box.html quoting the derived JT-60SA box and the limiter extent it comes from. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the committed revision the tests ran at and the full command with its PYTHONPATH, and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/eval/test_selene_reference.py tests/eval/test_efit_referee.py tests/worldmodel/test_equilibrium_labels.py tests/test_equilibrium_labels.py; it exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
